  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.94,
      "end_seconds": 7.62,
      "duration_seconds": 6.68,
      "text": "doctor, your next patient is here i've done the basics, I'll read them out in a moment"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.03,
      "end_seconds": 17.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Thanks, that's helpful. Hello, please sit. What's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 21.27,
      "end_seconds": 29.86,
      "duration_seconds": 8.59,
      "text": "ah, uh, good afternoon, doctor. I look after them so I thought I'd come"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.04,
      "end_seconds": 37.94,
      "duration_seconds": 6.9,
      "text": "So, I've been feeling well, and I wanted to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.69,
      "end_seconds": 42.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.87,
      "end_seconds": 59.06,
      "duration_seconds": 12.19,
      "text": "so, ever since... since last weekend, really. My family kept telling me to get it checked. It's the not knowing that gets to me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.35,
      "end_seconds": 63.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.41,
      "end_seconds": 77.12,
      "duration_seconds": 12.71,
      "text": "Hmm, when it starts I tend to get slightly dry skin as well. The slightly dry skin? That's been since last night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.97,
      "end_seconds": 81.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Did you notice any palpitations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.5,
      "end_seconds": 86.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Um, not that I've noticed, no palpitations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 87.39,
      "end_seconds": 93.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.88,
      "text": "actually, doctor, I did notice palpitations he doesn't always say"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.13,
      "end_seconds": 101.19,
      "duration_seconds": 7.06,
      "text": "Mm, no, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.02,
      "end_seconds": 111.61,
      "duration_seconds": 8.59,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. A few quick ones: constipation, feeling cold or weight change?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.55,
      "end_seconds": 117.94,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "I haven't had constipation, feeling cold or weight change, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.65,
      "end_seconds": 124.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.01,
      "end_seconds": 128.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "No, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.61,
      "end_seconds": 132.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.3,
      "end_seconds": 139.55,
      "duration_seconds": 5.25,
      "text": "Thyroxine. I take it 75 micrograms, maybe, every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.11,
      "end_seconds": 144.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "Do you have the packet or the prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.26,
      "end_seconds": 171.49,
      "duration_seconds": 25.23,
      "text": "well, no, it's at home oh, um, I take warfarin, 3 milligrams, in the evening for the blood thinning. Iron tablets, once a day i did try to ignore it for a while uh, um, before this I was on apixaban; that's been stopped"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.62,
      "end_seconds": 189.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Anything surgical in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.68,
      "end_seconds": 195.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "I had a bunion operation six years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.27,
      "end_seconds": 212.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.03,
      "end_seconds": 229.98,
      "duration_seconds": 15.95,
      "text": "I've had an underactive thyroid for about ten years now. Actually, I've had an irregular heartbeat for nearly five years now. Oh, I have low haemoglobin, for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.45,
      "end_seconds": 237.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.82,
      "text": "I see, go ahead. What does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.98,
      "end_seconds": 243.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.63,
      "end_seconds": 246.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.97,
      "end_seconds": 252.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.94,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.73,
      "end_seconds": 269.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.6,
      "end_seconds": 274.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "yeah, no, not that I know of"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 275.14,
      "end_seconds": 288.05,
      "duration_seconds": 12.91,
      "text": "okay, so the vitals from earlier pressure 108 over 78, temperature 36.7, weight 72 kilos, BMI works out to 28.5, respiratory rate 17, height 159 centimetres, saturation 97 percent, pulse 79."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.98,
      "end_seconds": 289.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.0,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.95,
      "end_seconds": 295.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "right, let's have a proper look at you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 297.33,
      "end_seconds": 299.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "Okay, um, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.8,
      "end_seconds": 303.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "hold that for a second"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.02,
      "end_seconds": 324.2,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "Your pulse is steady and your thyroid feels normal in size."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.9,
      "end_seconds": 339.67,
      "duration_seconds": 12.77,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed. So where does that leave us? I'd lean towards well-controlled thyroid replacement. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 341.36,
      "end_seconds": 345.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 346.31,
      "end_seconds": 366.37,
      "duration_seconds": 20.06,
      "text": "nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like well-controlled thyroid replacement. Keep taking the tablet on an empty stomach, apart from coffee. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 367.64,
      "end_seconds": 371.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Alright, um, thanks, take care."
    }
  ]
}